        {
            "id": "57560b17-145b-4a7b-8861-5078f42a33a6",
            "build_id": "26994b93-29ef-4dd0-8e7c-7fd243457e15",
            "round_number": 3,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-09T18:10:47.114898+00:00",
            "notes": "[Extendrils](item_138e73a2-6915-4ffc-bd89-029a85bf94b8) should be your first purple. Your goal is putting out a lot of orbs, and this will help them stay in effective range on friends and foes even longer.\n\n[Optimal Overflow](item_9d85ca48-b27a-435a-8ef9-247440e0f97d) is the choice for second power. If you're following the playstyle notes and using damage orbs most of the time, the damage orbs you'll send out with this power will help you keep your biotic energy charged and let you keep pumping heals into your allies. It'll create more pressure on the enemy team, too, causing a lot of incidental damage that'll force the enemy team to reprioritize their heals and reposition in the middle of hectic fights, usually making them less effective and forcing them to make worse decisions in the heat of battle.\n\nTry to position yourself so that you're standing behind your team and aiming your biotic energy heals forward onto your team, but in a way that your orbs will still be effective when they trigger. Don't forget to use your normal orb cooldown whenever it's up, too!",
