        {
            "id": "5733d323-b378-4190-92fd-2ccdb817b091",
            "build_id": "26994b93-29ef-4dd0-8e7c-7fd243457e15",
            "round_number": 4,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-09T18:10:47.114898+00:00",
            "notes": "[Superflexor](item_580b77b4-0d63-469b-99a8-5372c55dfc1b) is the next purple, it offers a ton of value and charges up from your biotic grasp (weapon damage) or biotic energy healing \u2013 not your orb. Because of how often your weapon damage/healing ticks though, it's easy to have it at max stacks the majority of the time.\n\nIf you feel like you *really* need the extra boost in biotic energy, you can pick up [Alternative Energy](item_c3e816b3-9c39-4528-9578-e3fa610b6cc6), but I find it to be a lower value pick that encourages bad habits. If you're using your damage orbs on cooldown, shooting the orbs from [Optimal Overflow](item_9d85ca48-b27a-435a-8ef9-247440e0f97d) even in the general direction of the enemy, and using your biotic grasp as a filler, you shouldn't find yourself running out of biotic energy when you need it very often. [High Capacity Tubing](item_d4779a06-a19c-425d-80ff-159fde15a3f2) or [Bio-Needles](item_fc8b5d34-98ab-412f-9e01-768d1986507f) are cheaper stop-gap solutions if you feel like you need just a little bit of extra help from keeping your biotic energy reserves from running dry.",
